    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n*** VIRTUAL TOUR AVAILABLE ***\n\nWest Winds is an impressive four-bedroom, fully detached family home, ideally positioned in the highly regarded Raheen area of Athenry. Offering generous accommodation, excellent outdoor space and a superb range of amenities close by, this property presents an excellent opportunity for families, first-time buyers or those seeking a comfortable home within easy reach of Galway City.\n* Site with Full Planning Permission adjacent to residence, also for sale. AMV 150,000 \n\nOne of the standout features of West Winds is the beautifully landscaped gardens, providing a wonderful outdoor setting. The property is also accompanied by a large garage and two separate sheds, providing an abundance of valuable storage.\n\nThe location is particularly appealing, with Athenry town centre and its wide range of everyday amenities within easy reach. Local facilities include primary and secondary schools, childcare services, shops, supermarkets, pharmacies, medical facilities, cafés, restaurants and a variety of sporting and recreational clubs. Athenry also benefits from an excellent rail service, with up on twenty daily connections to Galway and other destinations, making it an attractive choice for commuters.\n\nFor families, the combination of generous accommodation, landscaped gardens, extensive storage and proximity to schools and community facilities makes West Winds an especially attractive proposition. For commuters, the excellent road and rail connections provide convenient access to Galway City and beyond.\n\nWith its combination of space, privacy, practical outdoor facilities and an enviable location, West Winds is a home that offers both comfort and convenience in the heart of Athenry.\n\nFeatures:\n- Comprising of a c. 1,930sq, ft of living space\n-4 Bedrooms with an additional flexible room suitable for a home office, gym or playroom\n-Oil fired central heating\n-Within 5 minute walking distance to train station and town centre\n-Excellent public transportation links and motorway access\n-Schools nearby\n-Mature landscaped gardens\n-Site with FPP next door also available.\n\n\nDNG Leonard & Heaslip for themselves and for the vendors or lessors of the property whose Agents they are, give notice that: (i) The particulars are set out as a general outline for the guidance of intending purchasers or lessees, and do not constitute part of, an offer or contract. (ii) Any intending purchasers or tenants must not rely the descriptions, dimensions, references to condition or necessary permissions for use and occupation as statements or representations of fact but must satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of each of them. (iii) No person in the employment of DNG Maxwell Heaslip & Leonard has any authority to make or give representation or warranty whatever in relation to this development. DNG Maxwell Heaslip &Leonard accept no liability (including liability to any prospective purchaser or lessee by reason of negligence or negligent misstatement) for loss or damage caused by any statements, opinions, information or other matters (expressed or implied) arising out of, contained in or derived from, or for any omissions from this brochure."
      },
